# FDD 31 — Public Search. UNUSUAL SPLIT: this single FDD folder contains FOUR
# sub-numbered .docx files that genuinely span THREE different bounded contexts, not
# one — per fdd-review/CONVENTIONS.md's explicit call-out that FDD 31 (like FDD 17) may
# need splitting across domains. Kept as ONE file (not three/four separate files) since
# it's one FDD ingestion pass and the cross-references between the sub-documents (all
# three public-facing search features share one MiEdWorkforce landing page, confirmed by
# the same wireframe image appearing verbatim in the 31.1/31.2 docx) are worth keeping
# visible in one place. Sectioned clearly below by sub-document/domain:
#   - 31.1, 31.2 - Public Search - Educator Credential.docx -> credentialing (cred:)
#   - 31.3 - Public Search - Legacy Reports.docx            -> credentialing (cred:)
#   - 31.4 - Public Search - Pro Prep.docx                  -> epp (epp:)
#   - 31.5 - Professional Learning Search.docx              -> proflearning (plrn:)
#
# UNUSUAL IRI CONVENTION (noted per fdd-review/CONVENTIONS.md's instruction to flag
# deviations): Requirement IRIs here use each story's OWN domain's prefix
# (cred:Req_31_1_1, epp:Req_31_4_1, plrn:Req_31_5_1) rather than living uniformly under
# one FDD-review prefix — normally Requirements stay under the reviewing folder
# regardless of which domain satisfies them, but this folder genuinely spans three
# domains and giving each story its true domain's prefix keeps `grep`/SPARQL-by-prefix
# queries honest about which bounded context actually owns the work.
#
# Source material used: the .md sibling for each sub-doc (fast pass), then each .docx
# unzipped for comments.xml and word/media/*.png. 31.1/31.2 has 37 comments and 15
# embedded images; 31.4 has 33 comments and 5 images; 31.5 has 12 comments and 13 images;
# 31.3 has NO comments and NO embedded images (a one-paragraph "this doesn't exist"
# feature, confirmed by actually opening the docx, not just trusting the short .md).
# Nearly all comment threads across all three commented docs are already-resolved
# clarifications/corrections from the vendor-team/product-owner back-and-forth (Caswell,
# Ross, Groom, Dontje, Punniyamoorthy) — none surfaced a still-OPEN disputed point the way
# credentialing-fdd-11-16.ttl's "Define role" thread did; where a comment thread changed
# the acceptance-criteria text mid-review (e.g. cred 31.1/31.2 comments #34-47 on the
# search/minimum-input/pagination behavior), that's noted on the relevant Requirement
# rather than transcribed comment-by-comment.
#
# Granularity: each sub-document's own Addendum "Feature X.Y" numbered user stories are
# used as the Requirement unit (31.1.1-31.1.6, 31.2.1-31.2.9, 31.4.1-31.4.10,
# 31.5.1-31.5.13 = 44 stories across three docs), skipping each doc's separate "HIGH
# LEVEL SCENARIOS" paraphrase table (same content, coarser use-case numbering, no added
# traceability value — identical reasoning to the FDD 11/16 pilot). 31.3 has neither an
# Addendum story nor a scenarios table — its Business Specifications section is short
# prose, modeled as a single feature-level Requirement.
#
# Wireframes: 18 of the 15+5+13=33 total embedded images were extracted and viewed
# (not all — see the credentialing-fdd-11-16.ttl precedent for why full 1:1 cataloguing
# of every embedded image isn't always worth it). 31.4's and 31.5's first 5 images each
# map cleanly 1:1 to their doc's own explicitly-captioned "Wireframe N" list, confirmed
# by direct viewing — no offset issues like the FDD 11/16 pilot found. 31.1/31.2's first
# 5 images are a mix: image1/2/3/4 match "Wireframe 1-4" captions directly; image5 is
# uncaptioned but turned out to be the single most useful image in the whole FDD 31
# folder — the actual MiEdWorkforce landing page mockup showing all three public search
# entry points ("Educator Credential Search", "Professional Learning Opportunities",
# "Educator Prep Providers") side by side, which is direct visual confirmation that
# 31.1.1/31.4.1/31.5.1's landing-page-hyperlink stories describe one shared landing page,
# not three independent ones. images 6-15 in the 31.1/31.2 doc are a distinct, higher-
# fidelity revision pass (real MiEdWorkforce chrome/nav, not the rough boxed sketches of
# 1-4) depicting the same basic-search/no-results/credential-history screens with review
# annotations (red highlight boxes) burned in — 3 of these 10 were viewed (image6, 7, 15)
# to confirm the later revision didn't change any story's substance; the other 7
# (image8-14, minus the ones viewed) are further near-duplicate states of the same few
# screens (one, image8, is actually a stray Pro Prep filter-panel screenshot that leaked
# into the wrong doc) and were not individually catalogued.
#
# Validation: see this project's standard oxigraph load (ontology + full abox/mied-v3
# tree + this file) — zero parse failures, zero untyped satisfiedBy/oa:hasTarget targets,
# zero Requirements without a satisfiedBy or an Annotation, confirmed at the end of this
# ingestion pass.

@prefix sd:    <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:> .
@prefix oa:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix cred:  <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:> .
@prefix epp:   <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:> .
@prefix plrn:  <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:> .
@prefix pub:   <urn:solutiondesign:instance:publicportal:> .

#################################################################
# Source documents
#################################################################

